===== 2026-11-21 local API readiness reproduction =====
environment: same env as docker-compose.acceptance.yml api service; host
             Python 3.12.3, MongoDB 7.0.14, loopback Mongo, no container
result: /api/ready returned 503 while warming up, then 200 at 8s after start;
        boot reconciliation completed in 1.2s.
conclusion: application startup is not the cause. The failure is in the
            compose/container path, not in Nexus application boot.

===== 2026-11-21 acceptance readiness diagnosis (run 44855166233) =====
run: https://github.com/wicked-media/NexusMSP/actions/runs/44855166233
job: tenant-boundary-acceptance (136696121479), commit ef016fd
API container started 02:23:42Z. Captured before teardown:
  02:23:47.301 NexusOps API v3.0.0 started successfully
  02:23:47.440 NexusMSP boot reconciliation complete
  /ready 200 at 02:23:52Z, 02:24:22Z, 02:24:53Z, 02:25:23Z
  compose port api 8000 -> "invalid IP:0"
  compose exec api /api/ready -> status 200
  host GET http://127.0.0.1:18000/api/ready -> never connected
  host wait failed after 120s at 02:25:44Z
cause: docker-compose.acceptance.yml attached api only to the `acceptance`
       network with internal: true. Docker silently ignores `ports:` for a
       container attached only to internal networks, so the 127.0.0.1:18000
       mapping never existed. The API itself was healthy.
fix: api now joins `acceptance_publish`, a non-internal network used only for
     the host-loopback publish; mongo remains internal-only.

